# @DISTRO_NAME@: the developer README

## About this document

@DISTRO_NAME@ is a Linux distribution built from the Ubuntu [archive](#archive): Ubuntu @BASE_VERSION@ (`@BASE_SERIES@`) underneath, apt for packages, and on top a Wayland desktop made of Hyprland, Quickshell and the Omarchy shell, themes and fonts, ported from Arch to apt. @DISTRO_NAME@ works with Secure Boot on or off, with no key enrollment either way and never a requirement that Secure Boot be on, and @DISTRO_NAME@ installs onto an encrypted disk. The first machine @DISTRO_NAME@ is built for is a Lenovo Legion Pro 7 laptop with an Intel iGPU and an NVIDIA dGPU, so hybrid graphics and sleep are first-class concerns. @DISTRO_NAME@ is meant to run on other PCs too: Omarchy's fixes for other machines are applied at install where their device check matches ([docs/1, section 3](1%20-%20policy.md#3-omarchy-version-to-follow)).

Nothing is ever installed and then stripped out: the root filesystem is assembled from Ubuntu's archive one package at a time, and the parts Ubuntu doesn't have come from a small apt repository of our own. The Omarchy port is built up the same way: it starts from Ubuntu's configuration plus the parts of Omarchy the desktop needs to run, and each further Omarchy feature is added by a recorded choice ([docs/6](6%20-%20omarchy-port.md#choices)). This document, the developer README (`docs/README.md`; the repository's top-level `README.md` is the introduction for people deciding whether to install @DISTRO_NAME@), explains the tools that produce that repository and how those tools fit together. The reasoning behind each decision lives in the numbered documents next to this one in `docs/`.

